WEBVTT

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.190
There’s only 20 minutes left!

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.740
And it looks like everyone’s bread is almost done.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.000
Azuma...

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.410
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.330
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.630
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:27.000
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.260
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.060
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.580
Lots of nutrients!!

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.340
The sports bread showdown!

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.660
Kayser’s blue bread...

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.660
Suwabara’s red bread...

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.090
Okay!

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.410
It looks like everyone’s bread is done.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:32.310
Kayser said that Suwabara’s bread had a fatal flaw.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.830
Don’t tell me that Japan... will lose?

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:40.050
Without Azuma, we’re done for
if Suwabara’s bread loses.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.300
Hey, Ryou...

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.810
You don’t even consider the possibility that
Japan might be saved by Kawachi’s bread?

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.480
Not at all.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.060
Since it seems to me the
person himself doesn’t think so.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:51.560
All right then.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.110
I guess I’ll start the judging.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.070
Yeah, let’s start it.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.530
A-Azuma!

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.450
Hey, Kawachi! Suwabara!

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.660
I somehow made it in time.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.700
No you haven’t!

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.910
Not even 20 minutes are left!

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.210
You can’t even make microwave bread in 20 minutes!

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.500
It’s all right.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.170
I already finished making the bread.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:16.670
What was that?!

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.010
Then, hurry up.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.050
Hurry and bring it out.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.590
Don’t crowd me.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:22.890
I’m getting it out.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.390
Here. This is it!

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:27.930
Black?!

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.430
A black bread?

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.440
Is this <i>Japan</i> #51?

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.060
That’s right! This is <i>Japan</i> #51...

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.440
Hold it right there.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:36.940
Huh?

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.700
What is it, Old... I mean Mister Pierrot?

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.030
Sorry to interrupt you when you’re all
excited about introducing your bread...

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.450
but I can’t judge that bread.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.830
Why not?

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:48.950
Because I was late?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.660
No, according to the rules, as long as
you make the bread within the time limit,

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.830
being late isn’t a problem.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:55.960
But...

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.090
If you’re to suddenly bring in a completed bread,

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:03.470
you can’t prove that you’ve
made it within the time limit.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:07.350
More importantly, you can’t
even prove that it’s you who made it.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.470
Do you know?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.020
How long was the time limit?

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.780
150 minutes.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.690
I was easily within the time limit.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.740
I would have liked to see what you did, but...

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:24.700
I can’t possibly judge a bread
with so many unknown variables.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.200
I’m sorry, Azuma.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.200
It... It can’t be.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.620
Serves you right,
Japanese representative.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.620
But, even had you completed it within the time limit,

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.590
that filthy black bread could not have
won against my brother’s Blue Lagoon...

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:44.430
Did I not tell you not to speak?

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.720
You shameless creature.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.000
I apologize.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.560
That black bread...

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.850
While it appears to be black, it’s not burnt.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.730
And that luster...

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.490
How did he do that?

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:03.740
It’s interesting, and so it is a
shame that it cannot be judged.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.070
Wait!

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.080
Can’t you carry out the judging?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.780
It’s a lion!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:10.790
They’re putting on a performance!

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.580
No, it’s the King of Monaco!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.330
Y-Your Majesty!

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:17.750
The reason that the boy was late...

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.340
The fault lies with me.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.760
The boy arrived early in the morning.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.800
Did you find the ingredients that you were missing?

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:25.970
Yeah!

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.600
Thank you, Your Majesty.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:28.680
See ya!

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.050
Boy!

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.060
You plan on running to the arena?

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.810
Yeah, basically.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.770
Wait here for a bit.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.600
I am sure you will make it in time if you run,

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.650
but you might as well come with me in my car.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.780
Things went well up until then, but...

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.030
there was an accident ahead of
us and there was a traffic jam.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:48.780
Your Majesty!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.490
Don’t panic, Boy!

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.750
Wh-What is this?!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:06.670
Go on. If you use this portable bread workshop to make your bread, it will be all right.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:07.880
Amazing!

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.760
This car even has an oven attached!

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.770
In other words, I bear all the
responsibility for his being late.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:19.270
Could you not permit him to
participate in order to save me from shame.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.770
Hmm... Glance...

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.780
I have no objections.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:28.280
As a baker, I am interested in
knowing the nature of that black bread.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:32.280
As long as he has not cheated, there is no problem.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.370
Kawachi... Who are you guys fighting with?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.250
Kayser! It’s Kayser!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.170
He’s just changed his shape a little.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:44.130
I mean, how many weirdos do you see
wearing creepy masks like that?

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.090
A lot!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.050
Over there.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.800
Kayser! Kayser! Kayser! Kayser!

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.640
Oh yeah...
Kayser! Kayser! Kayser! Kayser!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:54.350
But, their enthusiasm is a little scary.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:57.350
It’s like the cheering squad for
the Hanshin Tigers at Koushien.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.640
Yeah...

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:01.230
It reminds me of the time when they won at Koushien.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.020
Why do you know about that?

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:08.070
Then, all of you cheering over here have
no objections to Azuma participating either?

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.070
None whatsoever.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.200
Gran’s the best!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.990
None whatsoever. It’s an easy win for Gran.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.950
We don’t even mind if every
baker in Japan is to participate.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.790
What obnoxious composure.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:24.380
I guess they don’t think that Gran could lose.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.590
I mean, no one but Gran from
the Kayser team has made bread.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:31.050
I guess they don’t have the slightest doubt that they could lose to someone like us.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:36.060
All right then. I officially permit Azuma
to participate and will begin the judging.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.060
Thank goodness.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.400
Then, let’s start with...

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.070
Kayser’s bread.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.240
Pi~errot.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.240
Well, if we’re talking about the Hanshin Tigers, there are “tora” patterns all over the place.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.620
Tora?
Note: Tora (<b>虎) is the Japanese word for tiger.</b>

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.030
That’s right. Tora.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.840
What are you doing?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:02.750
Now!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.370
Tora, tora, tora.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:09.210
You dumbass!

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.130
Tora tora tora.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.220
The surprise attack has been successful.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:17.010
And, Kayser’s bread has pearl powder in it.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:18.220
In other words...

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:27.480
Pearl! Pearl! Pearl!

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:30.650
A splendid bald pate... Just like a pearl.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.490
It’s all shiny.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:37.410
Why do I feel that everyone’s
gaze is intent upon my head...?

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.000
Could it be that there’s something on my head?

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.660
Wh-What?!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.080
My head!

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.750
There’s nothing on my head!

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.380
It’s a pearl.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.260
I didn’t leave anything behind.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:53.760
It was you?!

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.220
What do you mean a pearl?!

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.680
Why must I be subjected to something like this?!

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.760
Help me, Kayser’s bread!

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.270
Here, sniff on this.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.400
Aroma...

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.230
What’s this gentle aroma?

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.360
It feels like I’m in a field of flowers.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:14.330
Every nook and corner of
both my body and mind is relaxed.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:16.700
Oh yeah...

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.990
Wasn’t I angry about something?

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.670
I wonder what it was...?

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.040
Amazing!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.870
That angry Kawachi is all calm now.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:27.920
What in the world is...?

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.920
It’s the aroma of hydrangeas.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.420
Hydrangeas?

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:35.300
Kayser’s bread, Blue Lagoon,

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:40.100
in addition to blueberries and yogurt,
has a species of hydrangea called amacha

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:43.520
kneaded into the dough and onto the surface.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:49.060
Amacha is very fragrant and
has the effect of calming the mind.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:54.190
Kayser came up with this in order to reduce the nervousness a racer feels before the race.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:57.490
I’m sorry for Kawachi but...

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:01.200
I wanted to test its effectiveness
and I couldn’t help myself.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.740
It’s all right.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.200
Happens all the time.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.000
So don’t worry about it, Pierrot-chan.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.870
Okay! That’s what I’ll do.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.670
Works a little too well.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.710
Yeah...

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.340
I see! That’s what it was.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:17.630
Despite their name, blueberries are a dark purple.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:22.890
If just mixed with yogurt, while the dough may
have become a light purple, it won’t become blue.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.060
Hydrangeas.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:28.560
No, the pigment of amacha
is the reason that it’s so blue.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:32.360
Pearl powder, blueberries and hydrangea.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.530
All ideas that an ordinary
person could not come up with.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.030
Gran Kayser is a fearsome artisan.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.870
It’s a wonderful bread, Kayser!

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.950
Yep, yep.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.040
It’s really wonderful, Kayser-chan.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:50.670
In addition to pearl powder, to add in
amacha to reduce the nervousness of racers...

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.090
You can’t have a better sports bread.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:54.970
But of course.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.470
Kayser! Kayser! Kayser!

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:03.890
All right then.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.510
I’ll start judging the Japanese team.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.180
But whose bread should I start with?

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.690
Should I start with Kawachi?

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:10.900
Don’t bother.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.940
My bread has no chance of winning.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:16.650
Me!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:22.700
While it might be essential to
reduce nervousness before a race,

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:27.490
it’s even more important to
increase the competitiveness of the racer!

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:32.670
This <i>Lupan</i> #6, made with the blood of the snapping turtle, is more suitable for an F1 racer!

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.670
Then, let’s judge it.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:38.380
Sniff sniff.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:41.840
Take it back.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:42.630
I don’t want to eat it.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.760
Y-You don’t want to eat it?!

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:48.640
And you call yourself a judge?!

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:53.150
Right now, more than a judge,
my heart is that of an F1 racer.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:59.860
Right now, my little heart just went “ba-dump” as it doesn’t want to eat this bread.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:01.610
Because of the red wine.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:07.910
As you know, F1 racers must endure
several more G’s than a regular driver,

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.420
and so they get drunk really easily.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:13.870
No matter how trace the amount, alcohol is taboo.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.090
What are you talking about?!

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.920
This bread has been baked.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.630
The alcohol content has all been vaporized.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.090
Perhaps.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.890
But that won’t cut it.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:30.230
Like I just said, my heart is that of an F1 racer.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:34.650
You think that a racer would want to eat bread with red wine before a race?

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:40.650
And to think that your motif is that of a slow turtle...

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.160
Of course I wouldn’t want to.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.580
Like I said...

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.460
If a half-baked baker like you wants to challenge me,

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:55.120
you’re just going to have
to be reincarnated.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.210
What a state of things this is...

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.130
After giving those arrogant warnings to Azuma...

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.420
But, a baker must always work to bake bread

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:07.720
by placing himself in the shoes of his customers.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.890
Otherwise, he can’t make something truly splendid.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.560
I’m sorry, Azuma.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.680
It appears that I wasn’t strong enough.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.350
What are you saying, Suwabara?

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:19.860
If it wasn’t for your advice,
I would have been in trouble!

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:22.780
Just like you, I wasn’t strong enough.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:23.860
But...

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:27.360
This <i>Japan</i> #51 Kai is different!

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.120
Kai?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.700
Yeah.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:34.620
It’s the ultimate bread that was reborn
when both our weaknesses were combined!

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:39.630
Because you were there, I was able to improve upon <i>Japan</i> #51 specifically for F1 racers.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:50.140
This is where our fight begins!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:11.580
Somehow...

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:15.580
I get the feeling that I’m the
only one left in a different world...

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.210
Oh well, it doesn’t matter.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:20.580
Then, I will judge Azuma’s bread.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:23.800
Sniff, sniff.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:30.010
What’s this fragrance which makes my stomach growl despite its unappetizing appearance?

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:31.270
What?!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.850
Could this bread be in the image of an eel?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.520
Isn’t that obvious?

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:39.190
More importantly, eat it quickly!

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.020
Quite some time has passed since I made it.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.270
It’ll get cold!

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.360
No, wait.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:48.780
Eel is not the only trick to this bread.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.360
Oh... Oh, I see!

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:51.240
I got it!

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.280
Forget that and eat it quick.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.990
Azuma...

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:59.290
You have to relax in this world, relax...

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.130
The truth behind the black color is nori!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.500
It’s wrapped with nori!

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.210
Nori?

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.510
What’s nori?

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:10.430
Nori is a type of seaweed or algae

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:14.890
which is eaten after it’s dried and pressed flat as paper.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.480
Nori has more vitamin A than spinach,

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.150
30 times the vitamin B1 present in sardines

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:24.900
and 20 times the vitamin B2 present in milk.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.900
Vitamin A keeps your eyes from drying out.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:31.200
B1 and B2 help to keep them from firing out.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:36.910
And so it’s a really essential food item
for racers who rely greatly on their eyes.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.000
But...

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.370
Its one flaw is that if you don’t eat it
quickly once it’s wrapped around food,

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.920
it loses its crisp consistency.

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:48.960
That’s why Azuma is so eager to have me eat it quickly.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.680
If you know that then eat it quickly!

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:54.890
Relax... Relax...

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.510
Hey, hey. Pierrot-chan.

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:01.350
I’m a big-hearted person, so I forgive most things...

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:05.190
but if you do something that causes
Japan a disadvantage, I’ll get angry.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:05.650
Uh-oh!

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:09.360
If you know its flaw, eat it quickly.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:10.360
Oh well...

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:13.410
The hydrangea-hypnosis is wearing off of Kawachi.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:18.410
There are still many mysteries to this
bread, so I wanted to observe it a little more.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.660
But, I guess it can’t be helped.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.690
He’s taking his time tasting it, isn’t he?

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:36.600
Nori, huh?

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:43.440
It could be that Pierrot is planning to
take his reaction to a whole new dimension.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.730
A new dimension?

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.860
What do you mean?

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:48.660
Watch and you’ll find out.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:50.650
Watch and I’ll...

00:16:58.580 --> 00:16:59.620
I see!

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:03.910
He was tasting it for a long
time in order to distract our gaze.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.670
What can it be?

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:12.550
I get the feeling that everyone’s
paying attention to my head again...

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:13.420
Kawachi!

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.510
Sorry about what I did earlier with Kayser’s bread.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:18.430
While not quite making up for my sins...

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.650
Look!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:20.430
Huh?

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.940
M-My head has hair again!

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:28.770
I don’t quite understand, but thank you, Pierrot-han!

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.980
It might be best if you don’t move too much.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:40.700
My hair has quite a good flavor. It’s pretty good.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.670
Nori, huh?!

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:48.170
A splendid response and reaction...
Just as expected of someone from Kansai.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.420
And if you do this...

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.680
H-He looks just like him!

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:58.680
Rock-paper-scissors.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.430
What are you making me do, you idiot?!

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.970
Got a little carried away.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.480
I guess I was a little mean.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:05.770
A truly mean joke.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:09.190
Either way, it was an amazing bread, Azuma!

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:10.650
Right?

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.830
With this, I have finished sampling all the breads.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:18.660
This time I really need to make a difficult decision.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.120
I don’t think that Kawachi’s bread has been...

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:21.660
Shh.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:25.630
It was delicious, but I’m sorry to say...

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.250
Kayser.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:32.460
The Japanese representatives are going to the finals!

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:34.750
We did it Suwabara!

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:36.300
Yes!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.090
It can’t be!

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.590
Impossible!

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.100
Don’t mess with us, Pierrot!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.100
You fraud!

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:45.600
Did you get bribed by Japan or something?

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.600
It looks like they might riot.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:53.360
When compared to Kayser’s pearl powder and blueberries, they’re nothing.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.610
Like we can accept something like that!

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:01.450
Everyone. The judge’s decision is final.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.870
I beg for silence.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.290
Azuma-kun.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.380
There are black soy beans
in it as well, right?

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:09.920
Oh, amazing.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.080
How did you know?

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:15.090
Because, the bitten portion was a light black.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:20.340
Like blueberries, black soy
beans are rich in anthocyanin.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:25.390
So, your bread beat mine since it
had black soy beans, eel and nori,

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.100
all of which are good for your eyes, huh?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:34.110
No, Azuma’s bread had one more amazing trick to it.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.110
It’s called silk powder.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:37.860
Silk powder?!

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.610
Protein that has been pulverized?

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:42.740
It’s not surprising that not many people know about it.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:47.620
These days, it’s almost a commonsense ingredient in the diet of sportsmen in Japan.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:54.380
And what he used is sasamayu, the highest quality silk.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.380
These cocoons contain high levels-of the pigment flavanol,

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:59.720
which comes from the mulberry leaves that the silkworms eat.

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:04.350
They contain 10 times the amount of antioxidants compared to that of regular cocoons.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:07.560
In other words, when it
comes to the theme of sports bread,

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.350
you won’t find a better ingredient than this.

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:17.770
Also, silk powder has an elegant
sweetness that melts within your mouth.

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:21.860
Like the black beans or hitsumabushi,

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:24.450
that elegant sweetness mixes in with the
flavor of the eel scattered within the bread.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:28.370
It makes you feel like you’re
eating the highest quality unajuu.

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:29.950
Himatsubushi?

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:32.880
I don’t quite get it, but for some reason I’m drooling.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:38.050
I hereby proclaim, on my name as a world-level judge,

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:42.510
that this bread here is the best as a sports bread both in terms of taste and content.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:47.480
Is it really true that the silk
we wear has so many merits?

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:50.810
You mean to say that the
Japanese people’s love for food...

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:54.900
surpasses that of us the French,
who are so picky about taste?

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:01.490
I’ve lost completely, Azuma-kun.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.110
The defeated must leave.

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:05.490
Farewell.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:11.910
After being tortured with all kinds of schemes
and cheating, all we get is a “farewell” in the end?

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:15.580
At the very least, Gran
probably fought us fair and square.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.080
What’s the matter, Kuro-yan?

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.500
You’re taking his side?

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:21.460
That’s not what I’m trying to do.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:24.510
To the French, the baking of
bread is like a national sport.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:30.010
For the French representatives to lose
to foreigners, especially to the Japanese...

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:34.020
They will have to live with fingers being
pointed at their backs for the rest of their lives.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:36.490
So let us be merciful.

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:38.610
Kayser...

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:41.200
Kayser!

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.700
Thanks for helping me earlier.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.280
Let’s fight it out with bread again sometime.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.130
I don’t believe it.

00:21:58.130 --> 00:22:02.300
To think that we actually beat <i>that</i> Kayser.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:03.920
Hey, Ryou...

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:08.800
Come to think of it, what was the new dimension of the reaction you mentioned earlier?

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:12.730
I get the feeling that we’ve already
seen the level that he showed earlier.

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:15.310
You’re naive, Sophie.

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:18.070
Look at Pierrot’s mouth.

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:22.610
The nori stuck in his foreteeth...

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:24.580
indicates the victory of the Japanese representatives.

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:29.000
It’s become a checkered flag, right?

00:24:07.060 --> 00:24:09.890
With Azuma around, the finals will be a piece of cake.

00:24:09.890 --> 00:24:11.060
I wonder...

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:12.480
America has the <i>Gopan</i>.

00:24:12.480 --> 00:24:14.600
Huh? What the hell’s a <i>Gopan</i>?

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:16.150
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.150 --> 00:24:18.730
A menace that exceeds the speed of sound!! <i>Gopan</i> #97!

00:24:18.730 --> 00:24:19.860
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.280 --> 00:24:22.610
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.610 --> 00:24:22.850
Pearl powder has more than 20 amino acids required for beauty.

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:27.240
Pearl Powder
Pearl powder has more than 20 amino acids required for beauty.

00:24:27.240 --> 00:24:27.620
The unequaled beauty Cleopatra
Pearl Powder

00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:27.950
Cleopatra
The unequaled beauty Cleopatra
Pearl Powder

00:24:27.950 --> 00:24:28.770
Also drank it

00:24:28.770 --> 00:24:31.590
used to dissolve pearl powder in vinegar or wine and drink it.

00:24:31.870 --> 00:24:34.130
Oh?!
